    "id": "train-1011",
    "question": "A carpenter is building a house. He needs 80 woodblocks to build it. If he has 8 logs that can make five woodblocks each, how many logs does the carpenter still need?",
    "gold": "8",
    "answer": "The carpenter initially has 8 x 5 = <<8*5=40>>40 blocks of wood.\nSo he still lacks 80 - 40 = <<80-40=40>>40 blocks of wood.\nTherefore he still needs 40 / 5 = <<40/5=8>>8 logs of wood.\n#### 8"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many logs the carpenter still needs, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of woodblocks that can be made from the 8 logs.\n2. Determine how many more woodblocks are needed after using the 8 logs.\n3. Calculate how many more logs are required to get the additional woodblocks needed.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total number of woodblocks that can be made from the 8 logs.\nEach log can make 5 woodblocks, so 8 logs can make:\n\\[ 8 \\times 5 = 40 \\text{ woodblocks} \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine how many more woodblocks are needed after using the 8 logs.\nThe carpenter needs 80 woodblocks in total, and he has already made 40 woodblocks, so he still needs:\n\\[ 80 - 40 = 40 \\text{ woodblocks} \\]\n\nStep 3: Calculate how many more logs are required to get the additional woodblocks needed.\nSince each log can make 5 woodblocks, the number of additional logs needed is:\n\\[ \\frac{40}{5} = 8 \\text{ logs} \\]\n\nTherefore, the carpenter still needs \\(\\boxed{8}\\) logs.",
